! mcp_bootstrap_p149.strap -- "THE ERROR DUMP ROUTINE", printed page
! 149.  docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.156, header read and not
! assumed: the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11011MCP
! CARD ID HB000001   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 149".
!
! THE COLUMN-HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD IS BLANK.  Rendered
! at 600 dpi across the full right-hand end of that line: the word
! LOCATION is printed and NOTHING follows it before the frame.  That
! is the p.83 / p.144 case, not a zero and not a number -- refused,
! not guessed (docs/transcription_workflow.md, step 1).  So the join
! to p.148 rests on line 4's printed SLC and on the two witnesses
! under THE JOIN below, and this page adds a third member to the
! "blank heading LOCATION" set: pp.83, 144, 149.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Forty-nine printed lines, forty-eight cards (HB000001..HB000048;
! lines 7 and 8 share HB000007).  Lines 1-3 are the asterisk box
! around the heading "***** THE ERROR DUMP ROUTINE *****" (line 2);
! line 4 is "SLC,$"; line 5 is "CNOP,"; lines 6-10 build the
! routine's table-of-exits word and its two reservations; lines
! 11-49 are thirty-nine instructions, every one of them CODE.
!
! The routine is the error dump that printed p.121's Program Table
! of Exits reaches by "VF,AEDMPT" -- p.121 line 6 prints
! "215666.40  217460.00+  VF,AEDMPT  -ERROR DUMP", which is this
! page's first word, named and addressed, printed on a DIFFERENT
! page.
!
! The body:
!   AEDMPT (line 6)  the exit word itself: 45 bits of control
!                    followed by the 19-bit half-word address of
!                    AEDUMP, extracted out of a branch (see THE
!                    EXT PAIR).
!   AEDUMP (line 11) the entry.  LV picks up AEDMPT+3 as the first
!                    word address (comment "-FWA(I)"), LX/SX swap
!                    index 4 between AEDMPA and AEDMPI.
!   AEDMP2 (line 14) the bounds check: two KV/BXL-BXH pairs against
!                    SPPLB / SPPUB send anything outside the saved
!                    PP bounds to AEDRET, then an SVA/TI/BD/LVE
!                    sequence saves the index registers through
!                    SLRBU+14.
!   lines 24-35      three LVE/V+I/SVA rungs that walk a value and
!                    then test it with BUSAZ / BADZ / BE.
!   lines 36-49      the second bounds check, against SPPLB and
!                    SMARK, then a KVI ladder that counts 3, 15 and
!                    15.32 and branches to AEDMP4.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN, CLOSED FROM BOTH SIDES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 4 PRINTS "217460.00 *  SLC,$", AND AN SLC EMITS NOTHING, SO
! ITS PRINTED LOCATION *IS* THE COUNTER ARRIVING FROM P.148.  This
! deck writes a hard "SLC,(8)217460.0" so it assembles standalone,
! which ASSERTS that origin rather than checking it (docs/
! transcription_workflow.md, "A HARD SLC CANNOT DISAGREE WITH THE
! ARRIVING COUNTER").  The printed value is recorded here and in
! the first !CHECK note instead.
!
! NEAR SIDE: printed p.148 (PDF p.155) ends at its line 30, a
!   half-word branch "217457.40  217372.10 00  B,SDISP", so the
!   counter leaves p.148 at exactly 217460.00.  (Read out of
!   docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt, which is a legitimate index
!   onto ANOTHER page.)
! INDEPENDENT: printed p.121 line 6 prints "215666.40  217460.00+
!   VF,AEDMPT -ERROR DUMP", and decks/mcp_bootstrap_p121.strap
!   already carries "AEDMPT SYN,(8)217460.00".  A different page,
!   a different card, the same word.
! FAR SIDE, A FALSIFIABLE PREDICTION: line 49 is a half-word KVI at
!   217510.00, so the counter leaves this page at 217510.40.  The
!   volume OCR of printed p.150 line 1 reads "217510.40  217526.32
!   00  BZXE,AEDRET", which is that value.
!
! THE SURVEY IS WRONG ABOUT THE FIRST LOCATION AND SHORT AT THE
! END.  It reported 31 rows, 227460.00..217504.4.  The page prints
! 49 lines; the first location is 217460.00 (the leading 1 read as
! a 2 -- confirmed at 1200 dpi, and confirmed again by p.121's
! VF,AEDMPT on another page), and the last is 217510.00, five rows
! past where the survey stopped.  Nothing fell off either end: the
! card-serial column runs unbroken HB000001 (line 1) to HB000048
! (line 49) and the frame below line 49 is blank.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE EXT PAIR -- THE ONE PLACE THIS DECK DOES NOT SAY WHAT THE
! PAGE SAYS, AND EXACTLY WHAT IT COSTS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 6, 7 and 8 build ONE 64-bit word at 217460:
!
!   line 6   217460.00   100100000000000   AEDMPT  DD(BU,45),0(.3)2(.11)1
!   line 7                                         EXT(0,18)
!   line 8   217460.55   0437147                   B,AEDUMP
!
! C22-6531 printed p.35 ("5. EXT 'EXTRACT'") and C28-6129's
! "2. ext--Extract": the statement FOLLOWING the EXT is compiled
! only so that a subfield of it can be taken; bits I..J are then
! "compiled in the position in the code where the EXT occurs", and
! the name gets the dds (BU, J-I+1, 8).  So EXT(0,18) deposits
! NINETEEN BITS and the branch on line 8 DEPOSITS NOTHING OF ITS
! OWN.  There is no half word of branch at 217461.00 to be found
! later and "fixed" in: the whole of line 8's contribution is the
! 19 bits printed as "0437147".
!
! The arithmetic, so the literal and the label can be re-derived
! against each other by hand: AEDUMP is line 11 at 217463.40, whose
! HALF-WORD address is 0o217463 * 2 + 1 = 0o437147.  Bits 0-18 of
! a full-word branch are exactly that half-word address (bits 0-17
! the word, bit 18 the half-word select), which is why EXT(0,18)
! takes 19 bits and not 18.
!
! WIDTH, MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED.  The DRZ on line 9 rounds up to a
! word boundary either way, so the page's own counter does NOT pin
! this width.  What pins it is the print: listing_oracle renders a
! bare-octal datum in ceil(width/3) digits, and a column-ink
! profile of line 8's field at 1200 dpi counts SEVEN glyphs
! ("0437147"), which is 19 bits.  Line 6's field counts FIFTEEN
! glyphs by the same measurement, which is the 45 of its DD.
!
! RESOLVED.  strap_asm used to refuse "EXT" and this deck carried a
! "DD(BU,19),(8)437147" substitution that threw the DERIVATION away
! -- it wrote the number the page COMPUTES from the label AEDUMP, so
! if AEDUMP moved the page would follow and the deck would not.
! strap_asm now implements EXT (C22-6531 printed p.35, C28-6129
! printed p.19), checked against IBM's own worked example in
! tests/check_ext_pseudo_op.py, and THE PRINTED FORM STANDS BELOW.
! The 19 bits are now derived from AEDUMP exactly as the page
! derives them.
!
! Corroboration that lines 7 and 8 really are one construct: they
! share one card, HB000007 -- the only repeated serial on the page.
! That is corroboration and not proof (p.130 and p.144 both carry
! two-statement cards that are not EXT pairs).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE "AC" BYTE ON LINES 19, 23 AND 29 IS "A0"
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! All three TI rows print a byte whose second glyph is open, and
! all three are recorded here as A0.  The argument runs from what
! PRODUCED the byte, not from the ink:
!
!  * The low nibble of a VFL full word is i2, the offset index of
!    the SECOND operand.  "TI,15,SLRBU+14.,$1" and
!    "TI,1,SLRBU+14.,$1" carry no parenthetical index there, so i2
!    is 0 and the byte ends in 0.  strap_asm agrees: assembled, all
!    three rows come out A0, and no variant of the printed
!    statement produces AC.
!  * POSITIVE CONTROL: printed p.135 line 16 is
!    "216625.40  216633.00 80  000004.02 AC  TI,1,WRESL1,SIOINS($12)"
!    -- a genuine AC, and it has the ($12) that makes i2 = 0xC.
!  * PRECEDENT: pp.130, 136 and 138 each resolved this identical
!    print the same way, and p.130 carries both cases on one page.
!
! The ink supports the reading without licensing it: line 23 prints
! its octal field "000021.C2" and line 29 prints "0C0021.C2", and a
! C cannot occur in an octal field, so these rows demonstrably drop
! ink on round glyphs.  Per docs/transcription_workflow.md that
! shows the row CAN drop ink and never that a particular glyph did,
! which is why the argument above is the one that decides.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS SETTLED, AND HOW
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) "DRZ", not "DR", on lines 9 and 10.  DR and DRZ print the
!     SAME BINARY OUTPUT (a reservation prints its COUNT), so no
!     !CHECK on this page can tell them apart and a passing run is
!     no evidence at all.  READ OFF THE INK at 1200 dpi: the
!     statement column prints "DRZ(N),2" and "DRZ(BU,32),1", with a
!     clear Z in both.  This is the p.136/p.137 failure mode and it
!     is the reason the crop was taken.
! (2) The leading digit of the page's first location is a 1.  At
!     1200 dpi line 4 reads "21746C.CC" and line 6 "21746C.00" --
!     open round glyphs in an OCTAL field, so 217460.00.  The
!     survey's "227460.00" is a misread 1.
! (3) "AEDUMP" on line 8 and "AEDMPT" on line 6: the D's print with
!     the straight left stem and squared corners that separate D
!     from C on this drum (1200 dpi).
! (4) "AEDMPT" is corroborated as a SPELLING by another page, not
!     just as an address: decks/mcp_bootstrap_p121.strap read the
!     same six letters off printed p.121 line 6 independently, and
!     tests/check_symbol_spellings.py groups the two at one bit
!     number and passes.  AEDUMP, AEDMP2 and AEDMP1 have no such
!     second reader and rest on the ink alone -- all four were
!     rendered at 1200 dpi and every D shows the straight left stem
!     and squared corners that separate D from C on this drum.
! (5) Line 6's datum "0(.3)2(.11)1" was handed to strap_asm exactly
!     as printed and compiles to exactly the printed
!     100100000000000: the field entries put a 1 at bit 2 (the "2"
!     ending at bit 3) and a 1 at bit 11, which is what those
!     fifteen octal digits say.  The statement and the bits agree
!     with no reading left over.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY ONE of the forty-nine line numbers carries an asterisk
! right after it ("7*", "49*").  That is the ordinary column, not a
! mark.  LINES 4, 9 AND 30 carry a SECOND asterisk after their
! LOCATION -- the familiar mark that pp.3/37/38/39/88/97/98/104/
! 105/124/136 also carry.  It changes no bit.  What it MEANS is
! still unexplained: the obvious guess, "the counter was
! discontinuous here", is refuted on this very page, because line
! 30's counter arrives exactly (line 29's TI is 64 bits from
! 217475.40 and ends at 217476.40) and line 30 carries the mark
! anyway, while line 23's TI, which also follows contiguously,
! does not.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS, EVERY ONE READ OFF ANOTHER PAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   SLRBU   215324.00  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p116.strap line 21
!                      defines it, "SLRBU DRZ(BU,64),29"
!   SPPUB   215324.00  p.116 line 22 "SPPUB SYN,SLRBU"
!   SPPLB   215324.40  p.116 line 23 "SPPLB SYN,SLRBU+.32"
!   SMARK   215012.40  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap line 46
!                      "SMARK VF", !SYM 215012.40
!   AEDRET  217526.00  printed p.150 line 24 (volume OCR),
!                      "217526.00  000040.10 00  AEDRET  B,OMCP"
!   AEDMPI  217527.00  printed p.150 line 26, "AEDMPI XW,AEDMPB,6"
!   AEDMPA  217530.00  printed p.150 line 27, "AEDMPA XW,AEDMPB,6"
!   AEDMPB  217531.00  the operand of both those XWs, and p.150
!                      line 28 prints 217531.00 as its own location
!   AEDMP4  217511.00  printed p.150 line 2, "AEDMP4 LX,4,AEDMPI"
!
! SPPUB and SPPLB are SYN'd off SLRBU here the way p.116 defines
! them, so the "+.32" relationship survives rather than becoming
! two unrelated literals.
!
! NAME COLLISION, REPORTED NOT TOUCHED: "SMARK" at 215012.40 is NOT
! the "SMARK" that decks/mcp_bootstrap_p28.strap and p37 carry at
! 2162.40.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." opened the
! second assembly of MCP after p.98 closed the first TAIL block, so
! the two are different symbols that happen to share a spelling.
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap is the one that defines the one
! used here.  AEDMPT already exists at this value in
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p121.strap (same value, no conflict); AEDUMP,
! AEDMP2 and AEDMP1 are new names no landed deck carries.
!
! BIT OFFSETS THAT ARE A CONVENTION, NOT A READING: AEDRET,
! AEDMPA, AEDMPI, AEDMPB, AEDMP4, SPPUB and SLRBU are SYN'd at
! ".0".  Every offset from 0 to 31 encodes identically in a branch,
! a KV, an LX/SX or a TI operand, so only bit 32 -- the half word
! -- is observable from this page, and it IS checked (SPPLB at .40
! and SMARK at .40 both show, and both pass).  The bit WITHIN the
! half word comes from the defining cards cited above.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ASSEMBLER LIMITATION HIT: ONE, AND IT IS "EXT".
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "EXT(0,18)" is refused outright -- strap_asm.py line 2125 raises
! "pseudo-operation EXT not implemented by this assembler yet",
! and its module docstring lists EXT under "Not yet".  That is the
! substitution documented above.  EVERY OTHER PRINTED FORM ON THIS
! PAGE WAS HANDED TO strap_asm EXACTLY AS PRINTED AND ACCEPTED,
! including the ones that looked least likely: "CNOP," with the
! trailing comma, "DD(BU,45),0(.3)2(.11)1" with its two field
! entries, "DRZ(N),2" and "DRZ(BU,32),1", the bare index in
! "LX,4,AEDMPA" / "SX,4,AEDMPI" / "LVE,1,$" beside the "$1" form on
! the same page, "V+I", "BUSAZ", "BADZ", "BZXH", "BXE", and the
! "$.32" self-relative operand.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

AEDRET  SYN, (8)217526.0             ! p.150 line 24
AEDMPI  SYN, (8)217527.0             ! p.150 line 26
AEDMPA  SYN, (8)217530.0             ! p.150 line 27
AEDMPB  SYN, (8)217531.0             ! p.150 lines 26-28
AEDMP4  SYN, (8)217511.0             ! p.150 line 2
SLRBU   SYN, (8)215324.0             ! p.116 line 21
SPPUB   SYN, SLRBU                   ! p.116 line 22
SPPLB   SYN, SLRBU+.32               ! p.116 line 23
SMARK   SYN, (8)215012.40            ! p.103 line 46

!  THE PAGE PRINTS "SLC,$" ON LINE 4 AT 217460.00.  Restated hard
!  so this deck stands alone -- see THE JOIN.
        SLC, (8)217460.0

        CNOP,                        ! line  5
AEDMPT  DD(BU,45),0(.3)2(.11)1       ! line  6
!  ---------------------------------------------------------------
!  SUBSTITUTION.  THE PAGE PRINTS TWO LINES HERE:
!        line 7                EXT(0,18)
!        line 8   217460.55    B,AEDUMP      -> 0437147
!  strap_asm does not implement EXT.  The nineteen bits the pair
!  deposits are the half-word address of AEDUMP (217463.40):
!  0o217463*2+1 = 0o437147.  The branch itself deposits NOTHING --
!  do not "restore" a half word at 217461.00.  See THE EXT PAIR.
        EXT(0,18)                    ! line 7   printed form
        B,AEDUMP                     ! line 8   extracted by line 7
!  ---------------------------------------------------------------
        DRZ(N),2                     ! line  9
        DRZ(BU,32),1                 ! line 10
AEDUMP  LV,$0,AEDMPT+3.              ! line 11  -FWA(I)
        LX,4,AEDMPA                  ! line 12
        SX,4,AEDMPI                  ! line 13
AEDMP2  KV,$0,SPPLB                  ! line 14
        BXL,AEDRET                   ! line 15
        KV,$0,SPPUB                  ! line 16
        BXH,AEDRET                   ! line 17
        SVA,$0,AEDMP1                ! line 18
        TI,15,SLRBU+14.,$1           ! line 19
        BD,$.32                      ! line 20
AEDMP1  LVE,1,$                      ! line 21
        SV,$1,AEDMPB+8.0             ! line 22
        TI,1,SLRBU+14.,$1            ! line 23
        V+I,$0,.32                   ! line 24
        SVA,$0,$.32                  ! line 25
        LVE,$1,$                     ! line 26
        V+I,$1,1.                    ! line 27
        SV,$1,AEDMPB+8.32            ! line 28
        TI,1,SLRBU+14.,$1            ! line 29
        V+I,$0,.32                   ! line 30
        SVA,$0,$.32                  ! line 31
        LVE,$2,$                     ! line 32
        BUSAZ,$.32                   ! line 33
        BADZ,$.32                    ! line 34
        BE,$.32                      ! line 35
        LV,$1,AEDMPB+8.0             ! line 36
        LV,$3,AEDMPB+8.32            ! line 37
        KV,$1,SPPLB                  ! line 38
        BXL,AEDRET                   ! line 39
        KV,$3,SMARK                  ! line 40
        BXH,AEDRET                   ! line 41
        KV,$3,$1                     ! line 42
        BZXH,AEDRET                  ! line 43
        SV,$2,$5                     ! line 44
        KVI,$5,3.                    ! line 45
        BXL,AEDMP4                   ! line 46
        KVI,$5,15.                   ! line 47
        BXE,AEDMP4                   ! line 48
        KVI,$5,15.32                 ! line 49

