!
! Lines 19, 23 and 29 are printed on the page with an OPEN second
! byte glyph, "AC"; they are recorded above as the A0 they compile
! to, for the reasons under THE "AC" BYTE.  Every other character
! above is as printed.
!
! Line 49 is a half word, so the counter reaches 217510.40 for the
! page that follows.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THESE CHECKS DO AND DO NOT ESTABLISH
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Forty-three rows print BINARY OUTPUT and FORTY-ONE carry a
! !CHECK -- lines 6, 8 and 11 through 49 -- together with all four
! of the page's own labels and all nine externals.  Lines 9 and 10
! are the two DRZs, which carry none for the house reason recorded
! beside them.  Lines 1-5 and line 7 emit nothing (three comment
! cards, a blank comment card, an SLC, a CNOP at a boundary, and
! the EXT whose bits are line 8's).
!
! THE REAL CHECKS OF THIS PAGE'S OWN COUNTING are the rows whose
! operand is a label defined HERE, because each only resolves if
! every intervening row's LENGTH is right:
!   line  8  the extracted 0437147 IS AEDUMP's half-word address,
!            and AEDUMP is line 11 at 217463.40 -- a forward
!            reference over the two DRZs
!   line 11  LV,$0,AEDMPT+3. prints 217463.00.  AEDMPT is line 6 at
!            217460.00 and the trailing period makes the "+3." THREE
!            WORDS, so the row is a backward reference over both
!            reservations.  What it lands on is line 10's 32-bit
!            DRZ, which is what the comment "-FWA(I)", first word
!            address, reads against.
!   line 18  SVA,$0,AEDMP1 -> 217471.01, and AEDMP1 is line 21 at
!            217471.00 -- a forward reference ACROSS the 64-bit TI
!            on line 19, which is the row that pins that TI's
!            length and its half-word start
!   lines 20,25,31,33,34,35  the "$.32" rows, each of which prints
!            its own address plus 32 bits and so checks the
!            location counter against itself at six places
!
! TAUTOLOGY AUDIT.  Nine externals, every one defined by a card on
! another page (see EXTERNALS); no row here checks a value this
! page itself supplied.  The one value this deck ASSERTS rather
! than checks is the origin, 217460.0, because the printed "SLC,$"
! had to be made hard -- and that is the value p.148's last line
! and p.121's VF,AEDMPT both independently give.
!
! WHAT NO CHECK ON THIS PAGE CAN SEE:
!   * DR vs DRZ on lines 9 and 10 -- settled off the ink only.
!   * How the 2 words + 32 bits of lines 9 and 10 divide between
!     the two rows -- ARITHMETICALLY (see the note above the
!     checks).  It is not entirely unchecked in MEANING: line 11's
!     AEDMPT+3. resolves to 217463.00, which is line 10's object,
!     so a wrong split would leave the address right and the named
!     object wrong.
!   * What mode letter "N" means in line 9's "DRZ(N),2".  strap_asm
!     accepts it and reserves 2 WORDS, which is what the page's own
!     counter does (217461.00 -> 217463.00), but no primary source
!     was located for the letter itself.  Nothing here depends on
!     it beyond the length, which is checked.
!   * The bit WITHIN the half word for the seven externals SYN'd
!     at ".0" (see EXTERNALS).
!   * Whether line 8's nineteen bits were DERIVED from AEDUMP or
!     written as a literal.  The page derives them; this deck
!     writes them.  They are equal today.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

!SYM   AEDMPT   217460.00
!SYM   AEDUMP   217463.40
!SYM   AEDMP2   217465.00
!SYM   AEDMP1   217471.00
!SYM   AEDRET   217526.00
!SYM   AEDMPI   217527.00
!SYM   AEDMPA   217530.00
!SYM   AEDMPB   217531.00
!SYM   AEDMP4   217511.00
!SYM   SLRBU    215324.00
!SYM   SPPUB    215324.00
!SYM   SPPLB    215324.40
!SYM   SMARK    215012.40
!CHECK 217460.00 | 100100000000000 | line 6 AEDMPT DD(BU,45),0(.3)2(.11)1 (printed SLC,$ on line 4 gives this page's arriving counter as 217460.00) | 45
!CHECK 217460.55 | 0437147 | line 8 B,AEDUMP under line 7's EXT(0,18) -- 19 bits, the half-word address of AEDUMP, DERIVED from the label as the page derives it | 19
! LINES 9 AND 10 GET NO !CHECK.  Their printed "000002.00" and
! "000000.40" are RESERVATION COUNTS in the BINARY OUTPUT column
! (2 words; 0 words and 0o40 = 32 bits), not storage contents, so
! there is nothing deposited for the oracle to read -- printed
! pp.84, 109, 114, 129 and 139 give their DRZ rows no !CHECK for
! exactly this reason, and the two that were written here FAILED
! as "assembled 000000.00 00" until they were removed.  Their
! LENGTHS are pinned in sum, not singly: the counter leaves
! AEDMPT's word at 217461.00 and must arrive at 217463.40, which
! is AEDUMP's !SYM and its !CHECK, so 2 words + 32 bits is
! checked and the split between the two rows is not.
!CHECK 217463.40 | 217463.00 30 | line 11 AEDUMP LV,$0,AEDMPT+3. -FWA(I) -- AEDMPT is line 6, +3 words
!CHECK 217464.00 | 217530.10 10 | line 12 LX,4,AEDMPA -- the .10 is LX's own operation bits
!CHECK 217464.40 | 217527.11 10 | line 13 SX,4,AEDMPI
!CHECK 217465.00 | 215324.40 90 | line 14 AEDMP2 KV,$0,SPPLB -- SPPLB is 215324.40, and the half word DOES show
!CHECK 217465.40 | 217526.32 42 | line 15 BXL,AEDRET
!CHECK 217466.00 | 215324.00 90 | line 16 KV,$0,SPPUB -- SPPUB is 215324.00
!CHECK 217466.40 | 217526.33 42 | line 17 BXH,AEDRET
!CHECK 217467.00 | 217471.01 D0 | line 18 SVA,$0,AEDMP1 -- forward over the 64-bit TI on line 19
!CHECK 217467.40 | 215342.00 80 000021.36 A0 | line 19 TI,15,SLRBU+14.,$1 -- a 64-bit instruction at a HALF-WORD boundary; printed byte reads AC, see THE "AC" BYTE
!CHECK 217470.40 | 217471.04 00 | line 20 BD,$.32
!CHECK 217471.00 | 217471.03 B0 | line 21 AEDMP1 LVE,1,$ -- bare index 1, as printed
!CHECK 217471.40 | 217541.03 30 | line 22 SV,$1,AEDMPB+8.0
!CHECK 217472.00 | 215342.00 80 000021.02 A0 | line 23 TI,1,SLRBU+14.,$1 -- printed byte reads AC, see THE "AC" BYTE
!CHECK 217473.00 | 000000.41 05 | line 24 V+I,$0,.32
!CHECK 217473.40 | 217474.01 D0 | line 25 SVA,$0,$.32
!CHECK 217474.00 | 217474.03 B0 | line 26 LVE,$1,$ -- the "$1" form beside line 21's bare "1", same bits
!CHECK 217474.40 | 000001.03 05 | line 27 V+I,$1,1.
!CHECK 217475.00 | 217541.43 30 | line 28 SV,$1,AEDMPB+8.32
!CHECK 217475.40 | 215342.00 80 000021.02 A0 | line 29 TI,1,SLRBU+14.,$1 -- the SAME statement as line 23, printed twice on one page; printed byte reads AC, see THE "AC" BYTE
!CHECK 217476.40 | 000000.41 05 | line 30 V+I,$0,.32 (location carries an asterisk although its counter arrives contiguously)
!CHECK 217477.00 | 217477.41 D0 | line 31 SVA,$0,$.32
!CHECK 217477.40 | 217477.45 B0 | line 32 LVE,$2,$
!CHECK 217500.00 | 217500.50 C6 | line 33 BUSAZ,$.32
!CHECK 217500.40 | 217501.10 46 | line 34 BADZ,$.32
!CHECK 217501.00 | 217501.40 00 | line 35 BE,$.32
!CHECK 217501.40 | 217541.02 30 | line 36 LV,$1,AEDMPB+8.0
!CHECK 217502.00 | 217541.46 30 | line 37 LV,$3,AEDMPB+8.32
!CHECK 217502.40 | 215324.42 90 | line 38 KV,$1,SPPLB
!CHECK 217503.00 | 217526.32 42 | line 39 BXL,AEDRET
!CHECK 217503.40 | 215012.46 90 | line 40 KV,$3,SMARK -- SMARK is 215012.40 and the half word shows
!CHECK 217504.00 | 217526.33 42 | line 41 BXH,AEDRET
!CHECK 217504.40 | 000021.06 90 | line 42 KV,$3,$1 -- $1 is the index-register word 000021.00
!CHECK 217505.00 | 217526.33 40 | line 43 BZXH,AEDRET
!CHECK 217505.40 | 000025.05 30 | line 44 SV,$2,$5 -- $5 is 000025.00
!CHECK 217506.00 | 000003.13 04 | line 45 KVI,$5,3.
!CHECK 217506.40 | 217511.32 42 | line 46 BXL,AEDMP4
!CHECK 217507.00 | 000017.13 04 | line 47 KVI,$5,15.
!CHECK 217507.40 | 217511.32 C2 | line 48 BXE,AEDMP4
!CHECK 217510.00 | 000017.53 04 | line 49 KVI,$5,15.32 -- a half word, so the counter leaves this page at 217510.40
